Upgrade procedure for OpenZFS

Source: https://github.com/openzfs/zfs, release tag zfs-VERSION
	(for example zfs-2.2.11).  The matching release tarball is
	https://github.com/openzfs/zfs/releases/download/zfs-VERSION/zfs-VERSION.tar.gz
	with a detached signature (zfs-VERSION.tar.gz.asc).  Both the
	tarball and the annotated git tag are signed by Tony Hutter,
	key 4F3BA9AB6D1F8D683DC2DFB56AD860EED4598027.  Check both with
	"gpg --verify" and "git verify-tag zfs-VERSION".

Only the "current LTS" series in upstream RELEASES.md is a candidate for
MidnightBSD.  Upstream release notes list the supported FreeBSD versions;
our kernel is roughly FreeBSD stable/13 (__FreeBSD_version 1305500), so
check __FreeBSD_version gates and newer FreeBSD KPIs before upgrading.

The vendor branch (vendor/openzfs) carries the upstream git tag tree,
not the release tarball (the tarball adds autotools output and
dereferences symlinks).  Tags are vendor/openzfs/VERSION.  The import is
merged into sys/contrib/openzfs with git subtree (prefix
sys/contrib/openzfs).  Nothing is pruned: there is no MIDNIGHTBSD-Xlist.

To upgrade to a new version:

1. Fetch the tag into a scratch bare repository
   (git fetch https://github.com/openzfs/zfs tag zfs-VERSION) and verify
   the tag signature.  Download and verify the tarball as well and check
   that every file the tarball shares with the tag tree is identical
   (symlinks in git are regular files in the tarball).
2. Create a worktree of vendor/openzfs, remove all tracked files, and
   extract "git archive zfs-VERSION" into it.  Stage with
   "git add -A -f" so that files matched by upstream .gitignore files
   (for example tests/zfs-tests/tests/functional/rsend/fs.tar.gz and
   etc/modules-load.d/zfs.conf) are included.  The scripts/zfs-images
   submodule gitlink is not imported (git archive does not export it).
   Compare "git ls-tree -r" of the commit with the upstream tag; the
   only difference must be the scripts/zfs-images gitlink.  Commit as
   "Vendor import of openzfs VERSION" and tag vendor/openzfs/VERSION.
3. git subtree merge -P sys/contrib/openzfs vendor/openzfs on master.
   Resolve conflicts against the local patch list below.  Afterwards
   diff sys/contrib/openzfs against the vendor tree and review every
   remaining difference: rename detection and backported fixes have
   produced silent bad merges before (a duplicated
   zfs_secpolicy_setprops() in module/zfs/zfs_ioctl.c and a duplicated
   cached-symlink free block in module/os/freebsd/zfs/zfs_znode_os.c
   during the 2.2.11 update).
4. Compare with FreeBSD's sys/contrib/openzfs on the stable branch that
   uses the same OpenZFS series, and carry FreeBSD-only fixes that do
   not depend on FreeBSD KPIs our kernel lacks.
5. Update the build glue outside this directory: sys/modules/zfs
   (Makefile, zfs_config.h, zfs_gitrev.h, static_ccompile.h),
   cddl/lib and cddl/{s,usr.}bin/z*, sys/conf/files, and the loader
   (stand/libsa/zfs, stand/defs.mk, stand/loader.mk and friends).
   Other consumers of the OpenZFS headers: lib/libbe, sbin/bectl,
   lib/libprocstat/zfs, lib/libproc, sbin/zfsbootcfg, usr.sbin/fstyp.
6. Build zfs.ko with -Werror on amd64 and i386, build world and the
   loader, and test on a scratch pool (kyua tests under /usr/tests and
   the upstream zfs-tests suite) before touching a boot pool.

Local patches applied on top of upstream (OpenZFS 2.2.11):

  - .gitmodules: removed, since the scripts/zfs-images submodule is
    not imported (MidnightBSD 757360b8fa).
  - include/os/freebsd/spl/sys/time.h: TIMESPEC_OVERFLOW() treats only
    i386 as having a 32-bit time_t, not powerpc (upstream bfb276e55c76
    by Jessica Clarke, via FreeBSD; MidnightBSD 1a56bf7003).
  - include/os/freebsd/spl/sys/vnode.h: vn_flush_cached_data() uses
    vnode_pager_clean_sync()/vnode_pager_clean_async() (FreeBSD
    64e869e9b93c; MidnightBSD 757360b8fa).
  - lib/libspl/include/sys/types32.h: struct timeval32 removed
    (upstream 88433e640ddb by Jessica Clarke, via FreeBSD; MidnightBSD
    8e2eb38b61).
  - module/icp/asm-x86_64/modes/aesni-gcm-x86_64.S and ghash-x86_64.S:
    emit .note.GNU-stack for all ELF targets, not just Linux (FreeBSD
    0e80562f15e3; MidnightBSD 0c4a039478).
  - module/nvpair/nvpair.c, nvs_xdr_nvp_op(): the parentheses around
    "(value_sz = i_get_value_size(...)) < 0" are fixed.  Upstream 2.2.11
    assigns the result of the comparison to value_sz, which defeats the
    following buflen check.  Fixed upstream in 2.4.  (MidnightBSD
    8401a6b685, SA-26:40 port.)
  - module/os/freebsd/spl/spl_taskq.c, taskq_tsd_set(): no
    fpu_kern_thread() on i386 (FreeBSD; MidnightBSD 757360b8fa).
  - module/os/freebsd/zfs/vdev_file.c: vdev_file_open() takes the
    cred_t argument added to vdev_open_func_t in 2.2.11 and passes it
    to zfs_file_open().  Upstream 2.2.11 only updated Linux and does
    not build on FreeBSD.  (MidnightBSD, 2.2.11 update.)
  - module/os/freebsd/zfs/zfs_ctldir.c, zfsctl_root_readdir(): set
    *eofp at end of directory (FreeBSD bbb515decc5c).
  - module/os/freebsd/zfs/zfs_vnops_os.c: zfs_readdir() sets *eofp to
    0 or 1 only (FreeBSD d5cd41f2f1cf); zfs_getattr() sets va_rdev to 0
    for files that are not devices (FreeBSD c2b39a756fe7; MidnightBSD
    757360b8fa); the out_locked label in zfs_freebsd_copy_file_range()
    is defined only with MAC (FreeBSD 4fe752ccb3f8).
  - module/os/freebsd/zfs/zfs_znode_os.c, zfs_rezget(): use
    vn_pages_remove_valid() from __FreeBSD_version 1300522 as FreeBSD
    stable/13 does (FreeBSD 0c5f290ed909; MidnightBSD 757360b8fa).
  - module/zfs/dbuf.c, dbuf_unoverride(): ASSERT(ptr == NULL) instead
    of ASSERT0() on a pointer (FreeBSD 2165931f74f5).
  - module/zfs/lz4_zfs.c: on FreeBSD, allocate the LZ4 compression
    context with kmem_alloc() (malloc zones) instead of a kmem cache
    (FreeBSD; MidnightBSD 757360b8fa, moved from lz4.c to lz4_zfs.c in
    the 2.2.11 update).  Identical to FreeBSD stable/14.
  - module/zstd/zfs_zstd.c: zstd_mempool_deinit() returns early if no
    buffers were allocated (FreeBSD; MidnightBSD 757360b8fa); the
    compression code is left out under IN_LIBSA for the loader
    (FreeBSD).
  - include/os/freebsd/spl/sys/simd_aarch64.h (no-op kfpu macros under
    _STANDALONE) and module/icp/algs/blake3/blake3_impl.c (OMIT_SIMD):
    needed to build blake3 into the loader as FreeBSD stable/14 does
    (FreeBSD).
  - include/os/freebsd/spl/sys/simd_arm.h: kfpu_allowed() is 0 on
    32-bit arm, since kfpu_begin()/kfpu_end() are no-ops there (FreeBSD
    d6e24901349d).
  - cmd/zdb/zdb.c (FreeBSD b5ce60dffd5d) and cmd/zfs/zfs_main.c
    (FreeBSD stable/14): printf format fixes.

Earlier local commits that upstream 2.2.11 already contains (dropped in
the 2.2.11 update): 89bd591a67 (gcc 14 warnings), 1427a9bea8 (raw send
key mapping leak), c01dd1b0bf (__deprecated in compiler.h; the file now
includes the LinuxKPI compiler.h), 887260d429 (clang 21), the rest of
