Notes:

  - Upgrade the loader before userland.  OpenZFS 2.2 adds pool
    features that the loader must be able to read: org.openzfs:blake3
    and com.klarasystems:vdev_zaps_v2.  vdev_zaps_v2 becomes active by
    itself as soon as it is enabled (zpool create or zpool upgrade with
    the new userland), so a boot pool can become unbootable with an old
    loader.  Also new in 2.2: head_errlog, block_cloning, zilsaxattr.
  - Block cloning: vfs.zfs.bclone_enabled (zfs_bclone_enabled) is 0
    in 2.2.11, as in FreeBSD stable/14, so copy_file_range(2) does not
    clone blocks unless it is turned on.  OpenZFS 2.4 changes the
    default to 1; decide again on the next major update.
  - zfs.ko built from 2.2.11 gets a -Wunneeded-internal-declaration
    warning in module/zfs/arc.c (arc_buf_is_shared) without INVARIANTS.
